# The test stack's coordinates (task 174; architecture.md §12.5.10) — the layer over `.env` every test process reads.
#
# **Loaded after `.env`, and it wins where both set a name**: the api's single-command test scripts pass
# `--env-file-if-exists=.env --env-file=.env.test`, and Node lets the later file override the earlier one while the
# earlier still supplies everything this one does not — every credential and secret stays `.env`'s. A chain of commands,
# Playwright and Compose read it through `tools/with-test-stack.sh`, and Compose publishes the test stack's ports and
# names its database from it (`infra/compose/docker-compose.test.yml`).
#
# **The database name differs from the dev stack's on purpose.** A test process that reached the dev server by mistake
# fails on "database esg_test does not exist" rather than writing to the developer's `esg`.
#
# **Committed, unlike every other `.env.*` here** (`.gitignore` names this one path): it holds no secret, and CI and
# every laptop must agree on it.
DB_PORT=5433
DB_NAME=esg_test
REDIS_PORT=6380
